  assistant: I have identified the root cause of the duplicate entry error when using AsyncSQLAlchemyMemory with parallel_tool_calls=True: concurrent insertions of messages create a race condition that leads to duplicate primary key conflicts.

The fix I applied replaces the usage of `session.add` for inserting messages with a MySQL dialect insert statement using `prefix_with("IGNORE")`. This will cause the database to ignore duplicate key errors instead of raising an IntegrityError when an insertion conf...
